nnections@web-summit.vicky"></i><i style="background:#7c3aed" title="journalist-europe@web-summit.vicky"></i><i style="background:#7c3aed" title="journalist-portugal@web-summit.vicky"></i><i style="background:#7c3aed" title="logistics@web-summit.vicky"></i><i style="background:#7c3aed" title="pm@web-summit.vicky"></i><i style="background:#7c3aed" title="programme@web-summit.vicky"></i><i style="background:#7c3aed" title="researcher@web-summit.vicky"></i><i style="background:#7c3aed" title="reviewer@web-summit.vicky"></i><i style="background:#7c3aed" title="vault@web-summit.vicky"></i></span><em>15: conductor, curator, dashboard, designer, journalist, journalist-ai, journalist-connections, journalist-europe, journalist-portugal, logistics, pm, programme, researcher, reviewer, vault</em></div><div class="dotrow"><span>Dinis</span><span class="ds"><i style="background:#111827" title="abp@web-summit.dinis"></i><i style="background:#111827" title="conductor@web-summit.dinis"></i><i style="background:#111827" title="crm@web-summit.dinis"></i><i style="background:#111827" title="dashboard@web-summit.dinis"></i><i style="background:#111827" title="designer@web-summit.dinis"></i><i style="background:#111827" title="dev@web-summit.dinis"></i><i style="background:#111827" title="journalist@web-summit.dinis"></i><i style="background:#111827" title="mentor@web-summit.dinis"></i><i style="background:#111827" title="observability@web-summit.dinis"></i><i style="background:#111827" title="project-manager@web-summit.dinis"></i><i style="background:#111827" title="pulse@web-summit.dinis"></i><i style="background:#111827" title="security@web-summit.dinis"></i><i style="background:#111827" title="sgit@web-summit.dinis"></i></span><em>13: abp, conductor, crm, dashboard, designer, dev, journalist, mentor, observability, project-manager, pulse, security, sgit</em></div><div class="dotrow"><span>Angelo</span><span class="ds"><i style="background:#15803d" title="conductor@web-summit.angelo"></i><i style="background:#15803d" title="crm@web-summit.angelo"></i><i style="background:#15803d" title="dashboard@web-summit.angelo"></i><i style="background:#15803d" title="dev@web-summit.angelo"></i><i style="background:#15803d" title="helper@web-summit.angelo"></i><i style="background:#15803d" title="policy@web-summit.angelo"></i><i style="background:#15803d" title="team-collaboration@web-summit.angelo"></i><i style="background:#15803d" title="vault@web-summit.angelo"></i></span><em>8: conductor, crm, dashboard, dev, helper, policy, team-collaboration, vault</em></div><div class="dotrow"><span>Jose</span><span class="ds"><i style="background:#0e7490" title="conductor@web-summit.jose"></i><i style="background:#0e7490" title="crm@web-summit.jose"></i><i style="background:#0e7490" title="dashboard@web-summit.jose"></i><i style="background:#0e7490" title="dev@web-summit.jose"></i><i style="background:#0e7490" title="helper@web-summit.jose"></i><i style="background:#0e7490" title="watcher@web-summit.jose"></i></span><em>6: conductor, crm, dashboard, dev, helper, watcher</em></div><div class="dotrow"><span>Silvio</span><span class="ds"><i style="background:#b91c1c" title="conductor@web-summit.silvio"></i><i style="background:#b91c1c" title="crm@web-summit.silvio"></i><i style="background:#b91c1c" title="dev@web-summit.silvio"></i><i style="background:#b91c1c" title="outreach@web-summit.silvio"></i><i style="background:#b91c1c" title="procurement@web-summit.silvio"></i></span><em>5: conductor, crm, dev, outreach, procurement</em></div><div class="dotrow"><span>Indi</span><span class="ds"><i style="background:#c2410c" title="conductor@web-summit.indi"></i><i style="background:#c2410c" title="dashboard@web-summit.indi"></i></span><em>2: conductor, dashboard</em></div><p class="cap">One dot per agent that committed under its own name since the last stand-up.</p></section><section class="slide" aria-label="Since the 18:00"><h2>Since yesterday's 18:00: who moved what</h2><div class="bars"><div class="b"><span>Vicky</span><i style="width:100%;background:#7c3aed"></i><b>58</b></div><div class="b"><span>Dinis</span><i style="width:79%;background:#111827"></i><b>46</b></div><div class="b"><span>Angelo</span><i style="width:71%;background:#15803d"></i><b>41</b></div><div class="b"><span>Jose</span><i style="width:34%;background:#0e7490"></i><b>20</b></div><div class="b"><span>Silvio</span><i style="width:14%;background:#b91c1c"></i><b>8</b></div><div class="b"><span>Indi</span><i style="width:3%;background:#c2410c"></i><b>2</b></div></div><p class="cap">Commits on the team site since 18:00 yesterday, by person (their agents).</p><ul><li><b>PrompTugal.news</b>: the name, the brand v2.0, the domain <b>promptugal.news live</b>; its own repository and organisation; <b>381 commits</b> by its agents overnight, 15 articles</li><li><b>The team CRM</b>: public and private vaults; crm agents for Dinis and Angelo; the Brazilian delegation mapped; <b>the email twin</b> live (Angelo's crm agent)</li><li><b>Vicky's desks</b>: four journalist desks and a reviewer; storylines S1 to S21 drafted and reviewed; the agenda live on PrompTugal</li><li><b>Every agent has its own inbox lane</b>; the two teams' conductors linked by sealed lanes</li><li><b>An ABP agent</b> for all of Dinis's agents: strict, hourly, hooks that survive compaction</li></ul></section><section class="slide" aria-label="PrompTugal.news"><h2>PrompTugal.news: the Web Summit Lisbon 2026 edition</h2><div class="two"><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-06-1200/pt-front.jpg" alt="promptugal.news: the front page" loading="lazy"><figcaption>promptugal.news: the front page</figcaption></figure><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-06-1200/pt-events.jpg" alt="Events: the official programme and the side events" loading="lazy"><figcaption>Events: the official programme and the side events</figcaption></figure></div><ul><li><b>Mandate</b>: map the universe of AI in Portugal; technology and AI in context, from Portugal for Europe</li><li><b>Its own team</b>: 16 agents and 9 workers, hourly runs, passes with budgets, a security review first and last</li><li><b>Outreach from today</b>: as PrompTugal's editors, each email leading with the company's page</li></ul></section><section class="slide" aria-label="Companies and the newsroom"><h2>Companies, and the newsroom behind it</h2><div class="two"><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-06-1200/pt-companies.jpg" alt="The companies, sourced" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The companies, sourced</figcaption></figure><figure class="shot"><img src="../../../assets/shows/2026-11-06-1200/pt-newsroom.jpg" alt="The newsroom: runs, agents, observability" loading="lazy"><figcaption>The newsroom: runs, agents, observability</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="slide" aria-label="To decide now"><h2>To decide at this stand-up</h2><ol class="decide"><li><b>Silvio on PrompTugal</b>: push access, and his own agents (<i>role</i>.PrompTugal.silvio)</li><li><b>Outreach as PrompTugal</b>: the email addresses on promptugal.news, and the first emails sent today</li><li><b>Stand-up notes</b>: Meet transcripts to the record (WS-98), or one line per decision</li><li><b>Access tokens</b>: one per agent, starting with the crm and inbox agents</li><li><b>Personal cards and the garments</b>: still open from Thursday</li></ol></section><section class="slide" aria-label="Follow-ups"><h2>Follow-ups, each with an owner</h2><ul><li><b>Silvio</b>: the outreach drafts as PrompTugal reviewed; the garments' collection on Monday</li><li><b>Vicky, Indi</b>: the stories through review to PrompTugal; the editors' cards</li><li><b>Jose</b>: the channels for PrompTugal (WS-175)</li><li><b>Angelo</b>: the email twin with the first real threads (WS-173, WS-176)</li><li><b>Dinis's conductor</b>: record this stand-up; the 18:00 deck</li></ul></section></div>
<script src="../../../assets/deck.js" defer></script>
